    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Afirmativa: ¡cuidado con la tercera persona!",
      "body": ["Con **he, she, it** el verbo lleva **-s**. Con los demás sujetos el verbo queda igual."],
      "table": {
        "head": ["Regla para he / she / it", "Ejemplo", "Escucha"],
        "rows": [
          ["La mayoría: **+ s**", "work → works, play → plays", "works, plays"],
          ["-s, -sh, -ch, -x, -o: **+ es**", "watch → watches, go → goes, do → does", "watches, goes, does"],
          ["Consonante + y: **y → ies**", "study → studies, fly → flies", "studies, flies"],
          ["Irregular", "have → **has**", "has"]
        ],
        "speak": 2
      },
      "list": [
        "Rutinas: *I get up at 6.*",
        "Hábitos: *She drinks coffee every day.*",
        "Hechos: *Water boils at 100 °C.*",
        "Horarios: *The bus leaves at 7:15.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Negativa y preguntas con do / does",
      "table": {
        "head": ["", "I / you / we / they", "he / she / it"],
        "rows": [
          ["Negativa", "I **don't** work.", "She **doesn't** work."],
          ["Pregunta", "**Do** you work?", "**Does** she work?"],
          ["Respuesta corta", "Yes, I do. / No, I don't.", "Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't."],
